  "slug": "platform-resistance-9e33",
  "summary": "Recent October 2026 releases add curated, downloadable resources for peptides, plastic-degrading enzymes, immune escape and arthropod cuticle proteins.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is curated, downloadable knowledgebases that consolidate literature-derived or public data into standardized, searchable records. PAZy expands to over 450 experimentally validated plastic-active enzymes with added metadata and LLM-assisted curation. TTPdb consolidates 5366 targeted therapeutic peptides with 3D structures, binding data and disease links, while ProPepBA provides 3962 experimental protein-peptide affinities plus 608 chemically modified peptide records cross-linked to UniProt. PeptidomicsDB standardizes reanalysis of 151 public peptidomics projects (3992 samples) into more than 33M peptide records. ImmunEscpMap links immune-escape evidence across 667 source genes in cancer and viral infection. N-Zinclopedia provides predicted transition metal-binding sites and candidate metalloenzymes, and the accessible surfaceome work uses an agentic LLM pipeline to curate 1,783 canonical surface proteins. Cuticulome.org adds standardized nomenclature for arthropod cuticle proteins.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-10-25"
}
